# Firebase web config for local development. Copy to `apps/web/.env`.
#
# Vite reads this file from the app root and substitutes the values into the
# client bundle at build time. Without them the app still builds and every
# public page renders, but sign-in fails with "Sign-in is unavailable right
# now." — see `src/app/auth/firebase-config.ts` for why that is a null rather
# than a crash.
#
# These four values are public by design: they identify the Firebase project,
# they ship inside the bundle, and browser security rests on Auth and security
# rules instead. Real secrets (Stripe, Resend, the lookup token) belong in
# Secret Manager, never here.
#
# The values below are the `upskills-network` production project, which is also
# what the deployed build uses. Point them at your own Firebase project if you
# do not want local sign-ins landing in production Auth.
#
# `VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID` names the `WebApp` registration. The project briefly
# had a second web app; it is gone, and the id here is the surviving one. Auth
# does not actually read the app id — the api key and auth domain carry the
# request — but a stale id is a trap the day Analytics or Crashlytics is wired
# to it, so it is kept accurate.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyCJrR1GdAudqeB8JapcSOCA2Ln7CKNL7bU
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=upskills-network.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=upskills-network
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:694973978627:web:ac397327a3143b92e99636

# Cloud Storage bucket holding user-uploaded media (event hero images).
#
# Unlike the four values above this one is read on the SERVER, not compiled into
# the client bundle, so it has no `VITE_` prefix and Vite does not substitute it.
# `nx serve` does not export it either — pass it on the command line when you
# need to exercise an upload locally:
#
#   MEDIA_BUCKET=upskills-network-media pnpm nx serve web
#
# The bucket is public-read by design and is the same one the deployed service
# writes to, so anything uploaded locally is world-readable at its URL. There is
# no storage emulator, so there is no offline substitute.
MEDIA_BUCKET=upskills-network-media

# Shared secret authorizing `POST /api/v1/media/sweep`, the scheduled job that
# deletes hero images nobody ended up saving.
#
# There is no session on that request — the caller is Cloud Scheduler, which has
# no user — so this header value is the entire authorization. In production it
# comes from Secret Manager (see the `secrets` list in `apps/web/project.json`);
# the value below is a local placeholder and is not the deployed one.
#
# Leave it unset unless you are exercising the sweep locally. The endpoint reads
# it only when called, so an unset variable costs nothing until then.
MEDIA_SWEEP_SECRET=local-development-sweep-secret
